<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick William, Elector of Brandenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1620–1688</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Frederick William, the Great Elector, the Great Elector</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick William, Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, known as the Great Elector, ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a> from 1640. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> in 1648 he gained the secularised bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minden">Minden</a> and the reversion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a>, which passed to him in 1680. He built a standing army and a central administration that laid the foundations of the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="Frederick William, Elector of Brandenburg" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frans Luycx · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frans_Luycx_-_Frederick_William,_Elector_of_Brandenburg,_at_three-quarter-length.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
